<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Riksdag of Västerås (1527)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1527">1527</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Diet of Västerås</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riksdag">Riksdag</a> of Västerås of June 1527 was the assembly at which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustav-i-of-sweden">Gustav Vasa</a>, threatening to abdicate, forced the estates to transfer much of the wealth of the church to the crown and to allow the preaching of the Lutheran gospel. Its decisions, set out in the Recess of Västerås, broke the political power of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> and began the Swedish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> and the making of a Lutheran state church.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/riksdag-of-vasteras-1527.jpg" alt="Riksdag of Västerås (1527)" width="320" height="306" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Great_coat_of_arms_of_Sweden_(without_mantle).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
